@page
@model VERITAS.Pages.AboutModel

@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About VERITAS";
}

<section class="about-page">

    <div class="about-hero">

        <span class="section-label">
            ABOUT VERITAS
        </span>

        <h1>
            Evidence before<br />
            <span class="hero-accent">influence.</span>
        </h1>

        <p>
            VERITAS is an AI-assisted information verification
            platform designed to help users examine claims,
            evaluate evidence, and understand uncertainty.
        </p>

    </div>


    <div class="about-grid">

        <article class="about-card">

            <span class="result-card-label">
                01 — PURPOSE
            </span>

            <h2>
                Look beyond the headline.
            </h2>

            <p>
                Information moves quickly. VERITAS provides a
                structured way to examine claims before accepting
                or sharing them.
            </p>

        </article>


        <article class="about-card">

            <span class="result-card-label">
                02 — APPROACH
            </span>

            <h2>
                Evidence over assumptions.
            </h2>

            <p>
                VERITAS combines claim analysis, machine-learning
                signals, evidence retrieval, source analysis, and
                contextual information to produce a transparent
                verification result.
            </p>

        </article>


        <article class="about-card">

            <span class="result-card-label">
                03 — UNCERTAINTY
            </span>

            <h2>
                Not every claim has an immediate answer.
            </h2>

            <p>
                When available evidence is insufficient, VERITAS
                can return an UNCERTAIN result rather than presenting
                an unsupported conclusion as fact.
            </p>

        </article>


        <article class="about-card">

            <span class="result-card-label">
                04 — MEDIA LITERACY
            </span>

            <h2>
                Verification is a skill.
            </h2>

            <p>
                VERITAS also helps users develop practical media
                literacy skills, including source identification,
                context checking, cross-verification, and evidence
                evaluation.
            </p>

        </article>

    </div>


    <div class="about-method">

        <span class="section-label">
            VERIFICATION MODEL
        </span>

        <h2>
            From claim to conclusion.
        </h2>

        <div class="about-flow">

            <div>
                <span>01</span>
                <strong>CLAIM</strong>
                <p>Identify the statement being examined.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
                <span>02</span>
                <strong>ANALYSIS</strong>
                <p>Analyze the claim using available signals.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
                <span>03</span>
                <strong>EVIDENCE</strong>
                <p>Examine relevant supporting or contradicting evidence.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
                <span>04</span>
                <strong>VERIFICATION</strong>
                <p>Compare the claim with available evidence.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
                <span>05</span>
                <strong>VERDICT</strong>
                <p>Present a conclusion together with its confidence.</p>
            </div>

        </div>

    </div>


    <div class="about-principle">

        <span class="section-label">
            THE VERITAS PRINCIPLE
        </span>

        <h2>
            Evidence before influence.
        </h2>

        <p>
            A prediction is not proof. A repeated claim is not
            automatically true. Verification depends on the quality,
            relevance, and availability of evidence.
        </p>

        <a asp-page="/CheckNews"
           class="primary-button">

            Analyze a Claim

        </a>

    </div>

</section>